### rail-runs-annotate-refs.mts

=== S1 — One train segment, one run, unambiguous line. Trace: two station lookups then two line lookups, board before alight in both pairs.
S1.trace: [{"kind":"stations","lat":51.5,"lon":-0.1},{"kind":"stations","lat":51.54,"lon":-0.1},{"kind":"lines","lat":51.5,"lon":-0.1},{"kind":"lines","lat":51.54,"lon":-0.1}]
S1.out: [{"startTs":1100,"endTs":1300,"wayName":"Ayton → Ceeford · Alpha Line","mode":"train","pointCount":10}]

=== S2 — Not rail-like at all — no run, no lookup, segment passes through byte-identical.
S2.trace: []
S2.out: [{"startTs":1100,"endTs":1300,"mode":"walking","pointCount":10}]

=== S3 — refinedMode train alone makes a segment rail-like, even with mode driving.
S3.trace: [{"kind":"stations","lat":51.5,"lon":-0.1},{"kind":"stations","lat":51.54,"lon":-0.1},{"kind":"lines","lat":51.5,"lon":-0.1},{"kind":"lines","lat":51.54,"lon":-0.1}]
S3.out: [{"startTs":1100,"endTs":1300,"wayName":"Ayton → Ceeford · Alpha Line","mode":"train","refinedMode":"train","refinedReason":"station-pair upgrade","pointCount":10}]

