### rowshape-refs.mts
--- DATE: a plain date ships as a full midnight-UTC timestamp ---
DATE 2026-8-22: "2026-08-22T00:00:00.000Z"
DATE 2026-1-1: "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
--- DATETIME/TIMESTAMP ---
DATETIME 2026-8-21 23:15:0.0: "2026-08-21T23:15:00.000Z"
DATETIME 2026-8-21 22:15:0.0: "2026-08-21T22:15:00.000Z"
DATETIME 2026-8-22 16:30:59.0: "2026-08-22T16:30:59.000Z"
DATETIME 2026-8-22 0:0:0.7: "2026-08-22T00:00:00.007Z"
DATETIME 2026-8-22 0:0:0.70: "2026-08-22T00:00:00.070Z"
DATETIME 2026-8-22 0:0:0.700: "2026-08-22T00:00:00.700Z"
--- BIGINT: a JSON string, via the toJSON patch ---
BIGINT 7159200472543411371: "7159200472543411371"
BIGINT 0: "0"
BIGINT 1: "1"
BIGINT inside a row: {"log_id":"7159200472543411371"}
--- TINYINT(1): a NUMBER on the wire, not a boolean ---
as driver returns it: {"is_main_sleep":1}
if a host decoded bool: {"is_main_sleep":true}
--- ⚠ the same DATE column under a different process TZ ---
TZ=UTC           local midnight 2026-08-22 renders "2026-08-22T00:00:00.000Z"
TZ=Europe/London local midnight 2026-08-22 renders "2026-08-21T23:00:00.000Z"
TZ=Asia/Tokyo    local midnight 2026-08-22 renders "2026-08-21T15:00:00.000Z"
--- how JSON.stringify renders a number ---
120                      -> 120
17                       -> 17
100                      -> 100
0                        -> 0
0                        -> 0
1                        -> 1
-1                       -> -1
51.5696612               -> 51.5696612
-0.2786201               -> -0.2786201
0.5                      -> 0.5
-0.5                     -> -0.5
100000000000000000000    -> 100000000000000000000
1e+21                    -> 1e+21
1e-7                     -> 1e-7
123456789012345680000    -> 123456789012345680000
9007199254740991         -> 9007199254740991
0.1                      -> 0.1
1.5                      -> 1.5
2.675                    -> 2.675

